# The three-Oblivion-Ring loop again (CR 104.4b), but Bot2 holds Disenchant with two untapped Plains: at every priority
# Bot2 could cast it, so the loop contains an optional action and is no draw (CR 104.4b: "Loops that contain an optional
# action don't result in a draw"). Bot2 passes thirty times, letting the loop go round five times (two passes for each
# Ring that leaves, three Rings to a round), far past where a loop of mandatory actions is found; the game must still be
# going. Then Bot2 breaks it. After the thirtieth pass, as after the sixth, Ring A has just been exiled with Ring B and
# A's leaves ability (which will return C) is on the stack, B alone on the battlefield; Disenchant destroys B. B's leaves
# ability returns A, whose enters ability has no other nonland permanent to target and is removed (CR 603.3d); then the
# old A's leaves ability returns C, whose enters ability exiles A, whose leaves ability returns nothing (it is a new A,
# CR 400.7, that exiled nothing). One Ring is left on the battlefield holding one in exile, and the game goes on.

